{"parentUuid":"8931dbac-3372-488a-9ac9-7518243e17d9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"053b4cb6-ea8f-4d03-a982-971ae4c22c16","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EranRS3Vd3RxvxcmNHEUaP","type":"tool_result","content":"# Netlify serves the landing page from docs/. No build step.\n[build]\n  publish = \"docs\"\n  command = \"\"\n\r\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\nAccept-Ranges: bytes\r\nAge: 2\r\nCache-Control: public,max-age=0,must-revalidate\r\nCache-Status: \"Netlify Edge\"; fwd=miss; fwd-status=200; stored\r\nContent-Length: 739\r\nContent-Type: image/svg+xml\r\nDate: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:31:18 GMT\r\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 64\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"FirstRun\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e2c11355-1529-47d0-8a90-dbe4161ff4f4","timestamp":"2026-10-10T12:31:15.936Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Netlify serves the landing page from docs/. No build step.\n[build]\n  publish = \"docs\"\n  command = \"\"\n\r\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\nAccept-Ranges: bytes\r\nAge: 2\r\nCache-Control: public,max-age=0,must-revalidate\r\nCache-Status: \"Netlify Edge\"; fwd=miss; fwd-status=200; stored\r\nContent-Length: 739\r\nContent-Type: image/svg+xml\r\nDate: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:31:18 GMT\r\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 64\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"FirstRun\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8931dbac-3372-488a-9ac9-7518243e17d9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"D:\\Atharva\\firstrun","sessionId":"14c3df51-e6a1-4820-9ecc-9826c98f4212","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"56677924-a1ea-4755-815a-c7003cce9f74","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"053b4cb6-ea8f-4d03-a982-971ae4c22c16","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018J55fM2T578bkuZb4sBcyh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"GitHub Copilot coding agent runs in GitHub Actions powered environment opens pull request sandbox session logs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Assigning, tracking, and troubleshooting Copilot coding agent tasks\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/github-copilot-code-agent/3-assign-track-troubleshoot-copilot-code-agent-tasks\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent\",\"url\":\"https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/)\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent\",\"url\":\"https://github.blog/ai-and-ml/github-copilot/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent\",\"url\":\"https://github.blog/?p=87917\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent\",\"url\":\"https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/\"},{\"title\":\"using the copilot coding agent logs\",\"url\":\"https://help.github.com/en/copilot/using-github-copilot/coding-agent/using-the-copilot-coding-agent-logs\"},{\"title\":\"using the copilot coding agent logs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/using-github-copilot/coding-agent/using-the-copilot-coding-agent-logs\"},{\"title\":\"using the copilot coding agent logs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/fr/enterprise-cloud@latest/copilot/how-tos/agents/copilot-coding-agent/using-the-copilot-coding-agent-logs\"},{\"title\":\"AI & Agents\",\"url\":\"https://fast.io/resources/github-actions-copilot/\"}]\n\nYes, the query matches how GitHub describes the Copilot coding agent. It runs in a GitHub Actions-powered environment, opens a pull request, and records session logs you can review.\n\n**Workflow:** Assigning an issue to Copilot triggers the work. It then creates a dedicated copilot/ branch, opens a draft pull request linked to the issue, and begins an agent session inside a GitHub Actions-powered environment. Per GitHub's launch post, it boots a virtual machine, clones the repository, configures the environment, and analyzes the codebase using retrieval-augmented generation backed by GitHub code search.\n\n**Pull request updates:** The agent works in the open. As it works, Copilot pushes commits to the branch and updates the pull request body with status messages. When it finishes, a \"Copilot finished work\" event appears in the pull request timeline, and Copilot requests a review from you, triggering a notification.\n\n**Session logs:** To inspect the run, go to the pull request and open the session viewer. Click through to the pull request in the list, then find the \"Copilot started work...\" event in the timeline, and then click View session. From the command line, add the --log option. Optionally, use the --follow option to stream live logs as the agent works. GitHub's documentation also says during or after an agent session, you can inspect the session logs to understand Copilot's approach to your problem.\n\n**Stopping a session:** If you need to stop Copilot, click Stop session in the viewer.\n\nNote that the `gh agent-task` CLI commands are described as a public preview, and the agent-task command set is only available in v2.80.0 or later of the GitHub CLI. Those details may have changed since these pages were published, so check the current GitHub docs before relying on them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cc500d5f-011d-4b42-a20b-57de61186eef","timestamp":"2026-10-10T12:31:21.755Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"GitHub Copilot coding agent runs in GitHub Actions powered environment opens pull request sandbox session logs","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AzV9Q662KakeTXVnR7BBrk","content":[{"title":"Assigning, tracking, and troubleshooting Copilot coding agent tasks","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/github-copilot-code-agent/3-assign-track-troubleshoot-copilot-code-agent-tasks"},{"title":"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent","url":"https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/)"},{"title":"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent","url":"https://github.blog/ai-and-ml/github-copilot/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/"},{"title":"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent","url":"https://github.blog/?p=87917"},{"title":"GitHub Copilot: Meet the new coding agent","url":"https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/"},{"title":"using the copilot coding agent logs","url":"https://help.github.com/en/copilot/using-github-copilot/coding-agent/using-the-copilot-coding-agent-logs"},{"title":"using the copilot coding agent logs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/using-github-copilot/coding-agent/using-the-copilot-coding-agent-logs"},{"title":"using the copilot coding agent logs","url":"https://docs.github.com/fr/enterprise-cloud@latest/copilot/how-tos/agents/copilot-coding-agent/using-the-copilot-coding-agent-logs"},{"title":"AI & Agents","url":"https://fast.io/resources/github-actions-copilot/"}]},"Yes, the query matches how GitHub describes the Copilot coding agent. It runs in a GitHub Actions-powered environment, opens a pull request, and records session logs you can review.\n\n**Workflow:** Assigning an issue to Copilot triggers the work. It then creates a dedicated copilot/ branch, opens a draft pull request linked to the issue, and begins an agent session inside a GitHub Actions-powered environment. Per GitHub's launch post, it boots a virtual machine, clones the repository, configures the environment, and analyzes the codebase using retrieval-augmented generation backed by GitHub code search.\n\n**Pull request updates:** The agent works in the open. As it works, Copilot pushes commits to the branch and updates the pull request body with status messages. When it finishes, a \"Copilot finished work\" event appears in the pull request timeline, and Copilot requests a review from you, triggering a notification.\n\n**Session logs:** To inspect the run, go to the pull request and open the session viewer. Click through to the pull request in the list, then find the \"Copilot started work...\" event in the timeline, and then click View session. From the command line, add the --log option. Optionally, use the --follow option to stream live logs as the agent works. GitHub's documentation also says during or after an agent session, you can inspect the session logs to understand Copilot's approach to your problem.\n\n**Stopping a session:** If you need to stop Copilot, click Stop session in the viewer.\n\nNote that the `gh agent-task` CLI commands are described as a public preview, and the agent-task command set is only available in v2.80.0 or later of the GitHub CLI. Those details may have changed since these pages were published, so check the current GitHub docs before relying on them."],"durationSeconds":5.778843900000677,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"56677924-a1ea-4755-815a-c7003cce9f74","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"D:\\Atharva\\firstrun","sessionId":"14c3df51-e6a1-4820-9ecc-9826c98f4212","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9311114f-74fd-4b63-932b-503655ab5152","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"053b4cb6-ea8f-4d03-a982-971ae4c22c16","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YZ8T23cjmnKRRcPRxX9g1f","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Claude Code OpenTelemetry monitoring metrics events sandboxing docs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"claude code tracing\",\"url\":\"https://openobserve.ai/docs/integration/ai/claude-code-tracing.md\"},{\"title\":\"Observe Claude Code with OpenTelemetry\",\"url\":\"https://betterstack.com/docs/logs/claude-code/\"},{\"title\":\"monitoring usage\",\"url\":\"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/monitoring-usage\"},{\"title\":\"claude code tracing\",\"url\":\"https://openobserve.ai/docs/integration/ai/claude-code-tracing/\"},{\"title\":\"# Monitoring Claude Code Usage with OpenObserve and Querying via MCP\",\"url\":\"https://openobserve.ai/blog/monitor-claude-code-usage-openobserve-mcp.md\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code\",\"url\":\"https://last9.io/docs/integrations/claude-code/\"},{\"title\":\"claude otel\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/li0nel/claude-otel\"},{\"title\":\"claude code opentelemetry monitoring coding agents\",\"url\":\"https://lucaberton.com/blog/claude-code-opentelemetry-monitoring-coding-agents/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenObserve Docs\",\"url\":\"https://openobserve-website-preview.openobserve.ai/docs/integration/ai/claude-code-tracing/\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandboxing\"},{\"title\":\"docs.claude.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/sandboxing\"},{\"title\":\"code.claude.com\",\"url\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandboxing?via=sale\"},{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandbox-environments.md\"},{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandbox-environments\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code Sandbox Best Practices for Headless Runs\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.novita.ai/claude-code-sandbox-best-practices/\"},{\"title\":\"- Pourquoi Claude Code a besoin d'un sandbox en mode headless\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.novita.ai/fr/claude-code-sandbox-best-practices/\"},{\"title\":\"how to manage permissions and sandboxing\",\"url\":\"https://inventivehq.com/knowledge-base/claude/how-to-manage-permissions-and-sandboxing\"},{\"title\":\"Claude CodeのSandbox機能を改めて整理してみた\",\"url\":\"https://dev.classmethod.jp/articles/claude-code-sandbox-202604/\"}]\n\nHere's what the search turned up on both topics. I didn't open the pages themselves, so these summaries come from search snippets.\n\n**OpenTelemetry monitoring**\n\n- Anthropic's official monitoring page says Claude Code supports OpenTelemetry metrics and events. OpenTelemetry support is currently in beta and details are subject to change.\n- Metrics are time series, and events go through the logs protocol. Metrics are exported via OpenTelemetry's standard metrics protocol, and events are exported via its logs/events protocol.\n- Setup is done with environment variables. The docs show enabling telemetry, choosing exporters (OTLP, Prometheus, or console for metrics; OTLP or console for logs), and setting the OTLP endpoint and protocol.\n- Common metrics include session count, token usage (split by input, output, and cache types), cost in USD, and lines of code changed. Third-party guides also list commit and pull-request counts and tool accept/reject decisions.\n- Events include user prompts, tool results, API requests and errors, and tool permission decisions. Third-party guides say the events share a prompt ID, so you can reconstruct the sequence of one interaction.\n- Traces are a beta feature. Some third-party guides describe a per-turn span tree, but the official page is the authority on the beta status.\n- Third-party integrations (OpenObserve, Better Stack, Last9, and Grafana/Prometheus setups) are documented, and some say telemetry goes only to the endpoint you configure.\n\n**Sandboxing**\n\n- The official sandboxing page says Claude Code features native sandboxing to provide a more secure environment for agent execution while reducing the need for constant permission prompts.\n- Instead of approving each Bash command, you define which files and network domains commands can touch. The operating system enforces that boundary for every Bash command and its child processes.\n- The docs say filesystem and network isolation are both needed. They warn that without network isolation, a compromised agent could exfiltrate files such as SSH keys.\n- A Japanese guide says macOS uses Seatbelt, which is built in, while Linux and WSL2 use bubblewrap. It says WSL1 isn't supported and native Windows wasn't supported at the time it was written.\n- Sandboxing is separate from the permission system. Permissions cover tools such as Bash, Read, Edit, and WebFetch. Sandboxing limits what Bash commands can reach at the OS level, and a Read tool call may still reach files the sandbox blocks, since it still goes through permission approval.\n- The official docs also describe a \"dangerouslyDisableSandbox\" retry path. When a command fails due to sandbox restrictions, Claude may retry it with that parameter.\n- A separate docs page compares isolation options: the built-in sandboxed Bash tool, the sandbox runtime, dev containers, Docker, and VMs.\n\nFor authoritative details, check the official pages at code.claude.com/docs (the monitoring-usage page and the sandboxing page). Those are the most current sources, and the telemetry details may change while the feature remains in beta.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e9cd6326-bf35-4d66-958f-5c2193bc4cc4","timestamp":"2026-10-10T12:31:23.760Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Claude Code OpenTelemetry monitoring metrics events sandboxing docs","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DqjuiyAyf934cKoSBm5iaS","content":[{"title":"claude code tracing","url":"https://openobserve.ai/docs/integration/ai/claude-code-tracing.md"},{"title":"Observe Claude Code with OpenTelemetry","url":"https://betterstack.com/docs/logs/claude-code/"},{"title":"monitoring usage","url":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/monitoring-usage"},{"title":"claude code tracing","url":"https://openobserve.ai/docs/integration/ai/claude-code-tracing/"},{"title":"# Monitoring Claude Code Usage with OpenObserve and Querying via MCP","url":"https://openobserve.ai/blog/monitor-claude-code-usage-openobserve-mcp.md"},{"title":"Claude Code","url":"https://last9.io/docs/integrations/claude-code/"},{"title":"claude otel","url":"https://github.com/li0nel/claude-otel"},{"title":"claude code opentelemetry monitoring coding agents","url":"https://lucaberton.com/blog/claude-code-opentelemetry-monitoring-coding-agents/"},{"title":"OpenObserve Docs","url":"https://openobserve-website-preview.openobserve.ai/docs/integration/ai/claude-code-tracing/"}]},{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WJeL2f7S12fCAG2xuYHrKh","content":[{"title":"> ## Documentation Index","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandboxing"},{"title":"docs.claude.com","url":"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/sandboxing"},{"title":"code.claude.com","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandboxing?via=sale"},{"title":"> ## Documentation Index","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandbox-environments.md"},{"title":"> ## Documentation Index","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sandbox-environments"},{"title":"Claude Code Sandbox Best Practices for Headless Runs","url":"https://blogs.novita.ai/claude-code-sandbox-best-practices/"},{"title":"- Pourquoi Claude Code a besoin d'un sandbox en mode headless","url":"https://blogs.novita.ai/fr/claude-code-sandbox-best-practices/"},{"title":"how to manage permissions and sandboxing","url":"https://inventivehq.com/knowledge-base/claude/how-to-manage-permissions-and-sandboxing"},{"title":"Claude CodeのSandbox機能を改めて整理してみた","url":"https://dev.classmethod.jp/articles/claude-code-sandbox-202604/"}]},"Here's what the search turned up on both topics. I didn't open the pages themselves, so these summaries come from search snippets.\n\n**OpenTelemetry monitoring**\n\n- Anthropic's official monitoring page says Claude Code supports OpenTelemetry metrics and events. OpenTelemetry support is currently in beta and details are subject to change.\n- Metrics are time series, and events go through the logs protocol. Metrics are exported via OpenTelemetry's standard metrics protocol, and events are exported via its logs/events protocol.\n- Setup is done with environment variables. The docs show enabling telemetry, choosing exporters (OTLP, Prometheus, or console for metrics; OTLP or console for logs), and setting the OTLP endpoint and protocol.\n- Common metrics include session count, token usage (split by input, output, and cache types), cost in USD, and lines of code changed. Third-party guides also list commit and pull-request counts and tool accept/reject decisions.\n- Events include user prompts, tool results, API requests and errors, and tool permission decisions. Third-party guides say the events share a prompt ID, so you can reconstruct the sequence of one interaction.\n- Traces are a beta feature. Some third-party guides describe a per-turn span tree, but the official page is the authority on the beta status.\n- Third-party integrations (OpenObserve, Better Stack, Last9, and Grafana/Prometheus setups) are documented, and some say telemetry goes only to the endpoint you configure.\n\n**Sandboxing**\n\n- The official sandboxing page says Claude Code features native sandboxing to provide a more secure environment for agent execution while reducing the need for constant permission prompts.\n- Instead of approving each Bash command, you define which files and network domains commands can touch. The operating system enforces that boundary for every Bash command and its child processes.\n- The docs say filesystem and network isolation are both needed. They warn that without network isolation, a compromised agent could exfiltrate files such as SSH keys.\n- A Japanese guide says macOS uses Seatbelt, which is built in, while Linux and WSL2 use bubblewrap. It says WSL1 isn't supported and native Windows wasn't supported at the time it was written.\n- Sandboxing is separate from the permission system. Permissions cover tools such as Bash, Read, Edit, and WebFetch. Sandboxing limits what Bash commands can reach at the OS level, and a Read tool call may still reach files the sandbox blocks, since it still goes through permission approval.\n- The official docs also describe a \"dangerouslyDisableSandbox\" retry path. When a command fails due to sandbox restrictions, Claude may retry it with that parameter.\n- A separate docs page compares isolation options: the built-in sandboxed Bash tool, the sandbox runtime, dev containers, Docker, and VMs.\n\nFor authoritative details, check the official pages at code.claude.com/docs (the monitoring-usage page and the sandboxing page). Those are the most current sources, and the telemetry details may change while the feature remains in beta."],"durationSeconds":7.779120000001043,"searchCount":2},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9311114f-74fd-4b63-932b-503655ab5152","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"D:\\Atharva\\firstrun","sessionId":"14c3df51-e6a1-4820-9ecc-9826c98f4212","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
