{"parentUuid":"e72b6136-c3c5-4140-8219-fcf2194424c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CftZah3VZi8YkHyV3tcYx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #14 is open and I will merge it as soon as both test runs pass, which takes about 30 seconds.\n\n- **Placeholders gone:** every cell now has a real answer. For GitHub Agents I used the Copilot coding agent: it runs in an Actions-powered VM, starts from an issue, opens a draft PR and keeps session logs. For Claude Code I used its OpenTelemetry telemetry and its optional OS sandbox.\n- **Judgement calls:** these are my readings of the vendors' docs. For example, \"Partly\" for proving a fix means it only happens if you ask or script it. Check the ones you care most about.\n- **Icons and width:** the table is wider, with a yes/partly/no mark on every cell, an icon per row and per column, and a legend.\n- **Broken logo:** the logo file itself serves fine, so I could not reproduce it. I switched the table header to the inline logo, which cannot show a broken image.\n- **Docs file:** `docs/comparison.md` now matches the page.\n- **Hidden marker left:** one `FILL:tweets` marker remains as an invisible HTML comment in the build log, so it does not show on the page."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_read_input_tokens":439638,"output_tokens":384,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":368,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":439638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":368},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit